      "writtenOn": "2016-08-25T17:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is less readable. I don\u0027t like nil (or bool) literals in calls. They\u0027re harder to read.\n\nYou could at least pull this out into a variable for documentation, before the switch:\n\n   var signer crypto.Signer \u003d nil // automatic\n\nOr put a new variable in the acme package equal to a nil crypto.Signer:\n\n    cert, name, err \u003d client.TLSSNI01ChallengeCert(acme.AutomaticSigner, chal.Token)\n\nOr TLSSNI01ChallengeCert could take opts, like:\n\n    type TLSSNIOpt interface{ privateTLSSNIOpt() }\n\n    func WithSigner(signer crypto.Signer) TLSSNIOpt { ... }\n\n    func (c *Client) TLSSNI02ChallengeCert(token string, opt ...TLSSNIOpt) (cert tls.Certificate, name string, err error) {",
      "revId": "3f91868d1aa7d4901f36f172b46be9e7aab90c22",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "858566ca_e22e663c",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 435,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-25T20:48:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if I make TLSSNIOpt useful for some other methods as well? For instance:\n\n    type Option interface { privateOpt() }\n    func WithKey(key crypto.Signer) Option { ... }\n    func WithExpiration(exp time.Duration) Option { ... }\n    func WithBundle() Option { ... }\n\nthen:\n\n    client.TLSSNI02ChallengeCert(token, WithKey(key))\n    client.RevokeCert(ctx, cert, reason, WithKey(key))\n    client.CreateCert(ctx, csr, WithExpiration(time.Hour))\n    client.FetchCert(ctx, url, WithBundle())\n\nbut I would only add Option and WithKey in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "45d9ae0c_73cf9a60",
      "revId": "3f91868d1aa7d4901f36f172b46be9e7aab90c22",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0545f683_9ed79d4a",
        "filename": "acme/autocert/autocert.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 435,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-25T20:51:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can do both. You can make all \"type Option\" also be a valid \"type TLSSNIOption\" by embedding the Option interface in the TLSSNIOption option.\n\nJust be careful not to create Options which don\u0027t apply to everything that take an Option. That would be unfortunate, even if you rejected it at runtime with an error. I\u0027d prefer it to not compile.",
      "parentUuid": "858566ca_e22e663c",
      "revId": "3f91868d1aa7d4901f36f172b46be9e7aab90c22",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
